# =============================================================================
# scripts/.env — local credentials. Copy to scripts/.env and fill in.
#
#   cp scripts/.env.example scripts/.env
#
# scripts/.env is gitignored. NEVER commit it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: GITHUB SECRETS ARE THE SOURCE OF TRUTH, NOT THIS FILE.
#
# A deployed router gets its config from release assets rendered with GitHub
# Actions secrets. This file is read ONLY by scripts/deploy-local.sh and
# scripts/bootstrap.sh — i.e. one-time provisioning.
#
# Consequences, learned the hard way:
#   * Editing this file changes NOTHING on a router that is already deployed.
#     To rotate a credential: `gh secret set X` then publish a release.
#   * This file drifts silently. In one real deployment a WiFi password sat
#     wrong here for months while the router happily ran the value from the
#     GitHub secret — discovered only during a re-provisioning.
#   * After any `gh secret set`, update this file by hand to match, or the next
#     LAN provisioning will push a stale value.
#   * Secrets are write-only in GitHub. To see what is actually deployed,
#     download the rendered asset:
#       gh release download vNN --pattern 'engine__99-self-update.rsc'
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The variable names here must match column 2 of secrets.map.
# =============================================================================

# --- Required ----------------------------------------------------------------

# The repo the router polls. In CI this is derived automatically; locally you
# must state it. Format: owner/repo
GITOPS_GITHUB_REPO=

# Fine-grained personal access token used BY THE ROUTER to read releases.
# Create at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
#   Resource owner : you (or the org)
#   Repository     : ONLY this repo
#   Permissions    : Repository permissions -> Contents: Read-only
# Nothing more. This token lives in cleartext in a script on the router and in
# every release asset; scope it as if it will leak, because one day it might.
GITOPS_GITHUB_PAT=

# --- Optional: observability. Leave blank to disable. ------------------------

# JSON log sink. Better Stack example:
#   https://<source-id>.<region>.betterstackdata.com
GITOPS_LOG_INGEST_URL=
GITOPS_LOG_INGEST_TOKEN=

# Dead-man's switch. healthchecks.io example:
#   https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
# Strongly recommended: it is the only thing that alerts you when the router
# stops existing rather than when it reports a problem.
GITOPS_DEADMAN_URL=

# --- Local deploy target (optional overrides) --------------------------------
# ROUTER_IP=10.1.1.1
# ROUTER_PORT=2222
# ROUTER_USER=ci-deploy
# SSH_KEY=$HOME/.ssh/routeros-gitops
